 "notes": "Basic Scalar scenario (Figure 2). Constrains scalar field dark matter coupling to electron mass through changes in fine structure constant and electron mass. Signal coupling: (1/\u039b\u03b3 + 1/\u039be) where both photon (\u039b\u03b3) and electron (\u039be) couplings are involved; here reporting \u039be alone with \u039b\u03b3 set to infinity. Strongest constraints at 10^-13 to 10^-11 eV (\u039be \u2265 3\u00d710^19 GeV from paper conclusion). Data extracted from Figure 2 dashed line (electron coupling constraint). Conversion to canonical d_me using d_me = (M_Pl/\u221a(4\u03c0)) \u00d7 \u039be^-1 where M_Pl = 1.22\u00d710^19 GeV. Alternative scenarios (Dilaton/Modulus, Relaxion Halo) shown in Figure 3 but not extracted.",
